god_foreknows	one
foreseen_happens	one
free_will	one
impious_to_deny	one
# The known weak point in this reasoning is the scope of "necessarily" in P1 (S2).
# It could mean that the conditional is necessary: necessarily, what is foreseen comes to pass.
# Or it could mean that each foreseen event is necessary in itself.
# A1 and P2 rely on the second reading.
# But "necessarily" is a modal operator applied outside foreseen_happens, not a word inside the claim.
# The claim itself, that what providence foresees comes to pass, is read the same way in P1, P2 and A1.
# So I mark no change of sense and no bridge.
